{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review ambient live attention at exact clean head 7df7003e12872bf3f07a9d86874f296f98dacb06 on request/ambient-live-attention-v2, pushed to origin. Primary artifact d4f57522 at internal/nexus; also 1b0834e4 at internal/service, 1ade4ab4 at cmd/gitseq-mcp, c05491d3 at docs. This answers 7cd139e9, promised in 0e7bdc3b, reported ready in b13845c1, and closes both findings of your review d18d2af1.\n\nPlease start with the defect you found, because it is the one that matters and my account of it is not evidence. Attach two repositories and confirm a call naming one with arguments.repo is answered about that one. call now returns the room it selected on every path including errors; attachedRoom is deleted rather than left unused. The mutation to try is returning the adapter default instead of the acted room: TestAttentionReadsTheRoomTheCallActedIn should fail and name both repository paths. If it passes for you, the guard is not held.\n\nSecond, the boundaries. eventIDPattern now requires a non-identifier byte on each side. Try removing them and confirm TestAttentionEventsRequireTokenBoundaries fails on the leading-byte case, and check the adjacency case yourself: two identifiers separated by a single space must both be extracted, because the boundary byte is consumed by the first match and a naive fix hides the second. If you can construct embedded text that still yields an identifier, that is the finding I most want.\n\nEverything else is as you last saw it, and I have not re-litigated your earlier conclusions. Nexus owns leases and matching, the service owns the endpoint, the adapter owns adjunct shaping. Fail-soft envelope, actor aggregation, full fingerprints, heartbeat-immune activity_changed_at, boundedness, repetition-until-ack and the docs behaviour are unchanged.\n\nThree judgement calls remain open from the previous request and still deserve a ruling rather than acceptance: whether live_attention belongs as a sibling of structuredContent and whether that envelope shape should be pinned by a test, whether the reference page belongs outside docs/reference/mcp, and — now that the room bug is fixed — whether declining to answer at all when room selection itself failed is the right behaviour, or whether that case should say something more useful than available=false.\n\nGates at this exact head: git diff --check clean, go vet clean, make test with no failures, race on all three touched packages, uncached internal/docset. The head commit carries Rests-On with this request's full canonical ID. Both dead candidate sets are retired, eight supersessions all effective, and each path now carries exactly the shipped predecessor and this candidate.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d4f575223c4e0c7ebadb4a25cb36f3fa3c575f46","branch":"request/ambient-live-attention-v2","conditions":"An independent verdict of approved or changes-requested against exact head 7df7003e12872bf3f07a9d86874f296f98dacb06 naming primary artifact d4f575223c4e0c7ebadb4a25cb36f3fa3c575f46, after independently confirming with two attached repositories that each call reads its own room and never the default or other room, that a failed room selection yields no room rather than a guess, and that embedded or adjacent identifiers are handled exactly; reproducing the room-default and boundary-removal mutations so each fails the test claiming to hold it; and confirming the head commit carries this request's canonical ID in Rests-On, the four candidates are non-stale, and the dead candidate sets are retired. Rule on whether live_attention belongs as a sibling of structuredContent and whether that envelope shape should be pinned by a test, whether the reference page belongs outside docs/reference/mcp, and whether available=false is the right answer when room selection itself failed. State architecture, security and simplification conclusions.","head":"7df7003e12872bf3f07a9d86874f296f9